#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "CAP-SHARING Publication and sharing"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "External parties receive de-identified tables from a publication catalog over an open protocol, each share approved and registered."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: governance · depends on: [CAP-CATALOG]{1}, [CAP-CLASSIFICATION]{2}, [CAP-TRANSFORMATION]{3}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Data leaves the platform only as de-identified or aggregated tables, each approved and registered. This page covers sharing row-level data with partners. Open aggregate statistics are covered by [CAP-PUBLICATION]{1}, and a person's own records by [CAP-RECORDS.7]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Sharing protocols don't carry the provider's policies over to the recipient, so the protection has to be in the data itself ([P15]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "A publication catalog, built by the transformation layer."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "An open sharing protocol, a register of recipients, and a sharing panel."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "An identifier hashed without a salt can be reversed by trying every plausible identifier. Use a keyed hash or a surrogate key instead."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "CAP-SHARING.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Data leaves the platform only from a publication catalog of de-identified or aggregated materialised tables."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Every share's objects are in the publication catalog."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "CAP-SHARING.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Published tables enforce a minimum cell size by test, and replace identifiers with keyed hashes or surrogate keys, never unsalted hashes.{1}*Example:* A published identifier is a keyed hash, so someone holding a list of learner numbers cannot hash the list and match it; an unsalted hash would allow exactly that."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Publication models carry cell-size tests; no identifier column is an unkeyed hash."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "CAP-SHARING.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Sharing uses an open protocol, with recipients authenticated by federation where possible and otherwise by tokens rotated within a year."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "The recipient register lists each recipient's method and token expiry."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "CAP-SHARING.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Each share is a reviewed change sponsored by a steward, approved by a sharing panel, and listed in a published register."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Every live share traces to an approved change and a register entry."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "CAP-SHARING.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Shares name explicit tables, never whole schemas, and share no table history."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "No share includes a schema; shared tables have history sharing off."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "CAP-SHARING.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "SHOULD"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Researchers who need finer data work inside the platform, on a project basis, time-boxed."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-sharing.md
msgid "Research grants carry a project and an expiry."
msgstr ""

